{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the voice was heard in Pharaoh's house.</b> All Egypt already knew that Joseph had distinguished brothers in the land of the Hebrews, for he had told them; and now when they heard of their arrival he said, <b>And the thing was good in the eyes of Pharaoh and in the eyes of his servants,</b> for at first it had been a disgrace to them that a foreigner, a slave who came forth from the house of the Syrians, should rule over them, and now they rejoiced with great joy when they saw that he was distinguished and that all his father's household were distinguished." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> — <b>And the voice was heard in Pharaoh's house:</b> when his brothers recognized Joseph they sought to kill him; an angel descended from heaven and scattered them to the four corners of the house. At that moment Judah shouted with a great voice, and all the walls of the markets of Egypt fell, and they caused all the pregnant women to miscarry, and Joseph fell from his throne, and the mighty men who were standing with him turned pale, as it is said (Job 4:10): ״שאגת אריה וקול שחל ושני כפרים נתעו״; therefore you should say, ״and the voice was heard in Pharaoh's house״ — and this voice is none other than the voice of Judah, as it is said (Deuteronomy 33:7): ״שמע ה' קול יהודה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:27.151586738Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}